	(text "RADIO – socket for the lab-made E01-ML01SP4 breakout"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "077c7ce9-e30f-5e77-bebd-1c48da6b6717")
	)
	(text "The breakout plugs into J30 (its pins down, the SP4 on top) and is held by an M3 standoff at H30.\nVCC = 3V3_RADIO from the MCP1700 on the power sheet only (radio range 2.0-3.6 V, absolute max 3.6 V).\nPut J30 at the board end nearest the antenna wall and away from the boost module; the flex antenna's\nU.FL plug goes onto the SP4 (glue the plug for the drop test)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4a94523a-fa16-5c0d-b103-57339315ddaf")
	)
	(text "BREAKOUT SOCKET"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.1 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "57b5e3aa-4f8d-5f5d-ab76-d8a87f3b5b71")
	)
	(text "SPI SERIES RESISTORS (33 Ω, through-hole)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c969366c-dc3c-5a2d-9790-f1b5732c0282")
	)
	(text "33 Ω in SCK, MOSI and MISO soften the fast edges that travel down the 15 cm ribbon (less ringing).\nOn this one-layer board their legs are 10 mm apart, so another track may pass under a resistor body\nbetween its legs: the board drawing says which. A 0 Ω wire link can replace one if the bench shows no need."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
